NOTE ON PROVENANCE (added by dsh-guava-pack, not part of upstream):

The upstream package declares `"license": "MIT"` in its package.json and points at
the repository above, but ships **no LICENSE file**. This text is reconstructed from
that declaration so that the MIT notice accompanies redistributed copies, as MIT
requires. If upstream later publishes its own LICENSE, that file takes precedence.

This copy has been **modified** from upstream: only `lib/client.js` differs
(253 diff lines against upstream main, HEAD a3681ee, version 0.1.4). The changes add
persisted enable/disable preference, collapse the teardown into
startVisuals/stopVisuals, and restore the host `document.title` and favicon when the
theme stands down. The modifications are not authored by Tommy00748 and are likewise
offered under MIT. See ../LICENSES/README.md for the full inventory.

